aquinas-known-necessary.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 2 ways: aquinas-known-necessary.logic.r2 and aquinas-known-necessary.logic.r2.2 have "our_known_necessary" and "god_more_certain"; aquinas-known-necessary.logic.r2.3 has "our_known_necessary" and "god_more_certain" and "our_known_necessary ∧ god_more_certain → (known_by_god → □be)"; they differ when only "the future contingent thing is known by God", "even what we ourselves know must necessarily be" and "the knowledge of God is much more certain than ours" are true, which the first allows
